    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0279" n="187" xml:id="pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">War Department, Adjutant General’s Office, Cables
                    Section Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Adjutant General</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McCain</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Military Representative on the
                        Supreme War Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. For Secretary Baker:</p>
                <p>Reference cablegram 67 signed Bliss, the action of the President is as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>The President concurs in the joint note of the permanent military representatives
                    of the Supreme War Council in the sense formulated in your No. 67, March 28, and
                    wishes you to regard yourself authorized to decide questions of immediate
                    cooperation or replacement. March.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d126-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCain</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d126-f1" n="1" xml:id="d126-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Peyton C. March, Acting Chief of Staff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
